abstract: >-
  An openly licensed institutional toolkit for assessing and improving
  readiness for responsible AI use in research and research training.
  Operationalises the five-dimension competency framework and four-level
  maturity grid set out in Responsible AI in Academic Research: A Competency
  Framework for Research Training (Instats Policy Series, DOI
  10.61700/t31oy23grr) into instruments a university can actually run.
  Contains a twenty-cell institutional self-assessment scored across four
  axes (policy, people, systems, process); parallel researcher and supervisor
  surveys designed so the gap between what leadership believes and what
  doctoral candidates report becomes the finding; a gap-analysis worksheet
  with a named action for every transition between maturity levels; role
  briefings for executive research leadership, faculty deans, graduate-school
  leadership, research-integrity committees, and graduate-student
  representative bodies; a model institutional AI-in-research policy; an
  AI-use disclosure standard with ready-to-use statement templates; and a
  supervisor-candidate AI-use agreement built on a labour-versus-judgement
  task taxonomy. Licensed CC BY 4.0 so institutions can adapt every
  instrument, translate it, and embed it in local policy.
